                <pb facs="0869" n="759" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg759"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003/558: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-03-16T17:00:00-05:00">March 16, 1931—5
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>103. Your 131, March 14, 11 a.m. In view of Legation’s present statement, you
                    may, in your discretion, withhold issuing consular circular or so phrase the
                    circular that it cannot be interpreted as a criticism of Consul Stevens’ efforts
                    to prepare a report on the Chinese judiciary in Yunnan Province.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
